+          <dt pn="section-11.3-3.7">Optional parameters:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-11.3-3.8">None.</dd>
+          <dt pn="section-11.3-3.9">Encoding considerations:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-11.3-3.10">The native form of the data object is binary data,
+zero-padded to an octet boundary.</dd>
+          <dt pn="section-11.3-3.11">Restrictions on usage:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-11.3-3.12">This type is only defined for data object (stored file)
+transfer.  The most common transports for the type are
+HTTP and SMTP.</dd>
+          <dt pn="section-11.3-3.13">Security considerations:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-11.3-3.14">See Section 9 of this memo.</dd>
+          <dt pn="section-11.3-3.15">Interoperability considerations:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-11.3-3.16">None.</dd>
+          <dt pn="section-11.3-3.17">Published specification:</dt>
+          <dd pn="section-11.3-3.18">The audio/asc data object is the AudioSpecificConfig
